* sg13g2-bandgap -- closed-loop vref/TC PEX (post-layout) PVT testbench
* (issue #186, T1 tracker #4 item 7). Generated from
* sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt-pex/testbench/tb_closed_loop_vref_pex.spice.tmpl
* by sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt-pex/run_pvt_sweep.sh -- do not edit a
* generated netlist-snapshots/*.spice file directly, edit this template and
* re-run the sweep. Full rationale is in
* sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt-pex/README.md; this header is a pointer, not a
* restatement.
*
* Generated for: corner=sf temp=-40C vdd=3.63V
* DUT git sha (design/netlist/bandgap_core.spice, for XQ1/XQ2/XQ3, the
* only devices this bench still splices from a schematic):
*   core=d83f7c4 amp=397fe2d startup=66ac99d
* Layout git sha (layout/bandgap_top/bandgap_top.gds /
* bandgap_top.pex.spice, extraction input for every MOS/resistor device):
*   8abe2aa
* PDK: ihp-sg13g2 /home/ubuntu/share/pdk (see sim/pdk.json for the pinned release)
* OSDI models: /home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi (built by sim/tools/build-osdi.sh)
*
* THIS IS A HYBRID PEX NETLIST, NOT A PURE LAYOUT EXTRACTION -- read
* sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt-pex/README.md "What this does and does not
* model" before trusting a result here. Short version, same shape as
* sim/core-open-loop-bias-pex's own header, extended to the assembled
* closed-loop topology:
*   - Every sg13_hv_pmos/sg13_hv_nmos/rppd/rhigh device below is re-encoded
*     from `klt extract --deck sg13g2 --parasitics
*     layout/bandgap_top/bandgap_top.gds` (layout/bandgap_top/
*     bandgap_top.pex.spice, pex_extract_report.json): real drawn
*     W/L/AS/AD/PS/PD from the routed, ASSEMBLED layout (bandgap_core +
*     bandgap_amp + bandgap_startup wired together, exactly as
*     design/bandgap_top.sch specifies -- this is the first PEX experiment
*     in this tree built from the top-level GDS rather than a leaf cell).
*     Device instance names below match design/netlist/bandgap_core.spice,
*     bandgap_amp.spice and bandgap_startup.spice one-for-one (XM1/XM2A/.../
*     XMTAIL/XMP1-4/XMN1-4/XRPU/XMSENSE/XMKFB) -- confirmed by reading
*     bandgap_top.pex.spice's own M$1-M$17/R$18-R$20 cards and matching each
*     one's drawn geometry (w/l/as/ad/ps/pd) against the schematic device it
*     replaces, not assumed from card order. This is also why
*     .github/scripts/check_evidence_formats.py's DUT-freshness check
*     (sim/README.md "DUT freshness") can compare this bench's snapshots
*     against all three design/netlist/*.spice files directly: same
*     instance names, same models, same nominal w/l/ng/m -- the extraction
*     only ADDS as/ad/ps/pd (see that script's dut_signature() docstring).
*   - XQ1/XQ2/XQ3 (npn13G2) are NOT extracted -- klt's curated sg13g2 deck
*     still does not recognise bipolar devices (klayout-tools, filed
*     generically; layout/README.md's LVS section has the full writeup;
*     layout/bandgap_top/lvs_report.json's own `device.unmatched` count is
*     exactly 3, all Q1/Q2/Q3). Spliced in verbatim from
*     design/netlist/bandgap_core.spice, wired to the extraction's own real,
*     physically-routed net names (sns1, cb2, cb3, vss) -- not invented
*     nodes, same convention sim/core-open-loop-bias-pex established.
*   - Merged-net labels: the extraction reports three top-level pins as
*     merged labels -- `FB|OUT` (10 device terminals), `IN_N|SNS1` (3),
*     `IN_P|SNS2` (4) -- because design/bandgap_top.sch ties bandgap_amp's
*     `out`/`in_n`/`in_p` pins directly onto bandgap_core/bandgap_startup's
*     `fb`/`sns1`/`sns2` (design/netlist/bandgap_top.spice's own
*     `Xx2 sns2 sns1 vss fb vdd bandgap_amp` instance line), not shorts --
*     layout/README.md documents the derivation. Named here as `fb`,
*     `sns1`, `sns2` respectively (matching every schematic-level closed-loop
*     testbench's own net names) rather than embedding the extraction's
*     escaped `FB\x7cOUT` / `IN_N\x7cSNS1` / `IN_P\x7cSNS2` forms, per issue
*     #186's own guidance.
*   - Body/well ties are REAL here, not a testbench fixture: unlike
*     sim/core-open-loop-bias-pex (whose leaf-cell layout left PMOS bodies
*     on an anonymous single-terminal net, issue #158's well/substrate-tap
*     ring not yet having landed on that cell at the time), bandgap_top's
*     M$1-M$17 cards each report a genuine, distinct nb terminal on a real
*     multi-terminal VDD (pfet) or VSS (nfet) net, each through its own
*     wire-parasitic hub leg. This bench instantiates every device's body
*     hub leg exactly as extracted -- no FIXTURE-style body override is
*     needed or applied.
*   - XMKFB's drain is the one device whose current this bench explicitly
*     probes (i_mkfb, matching every schematic-level closed-loop testbench's
*     own measurement): a 0V ammeter (Vmkfb) sits between XMKFB's own drain
*     terminal and its extracted wire-parasitic hub node (fb__t1), so the
*     measured current is upstream of that leg's own IR drop, same
*     "ammeter measures the device, not a shared hub" rationale
*     sim/core-open-loop-bias-pex's FIXTURE 2 documents.
*   - Wire parasitics: every other net (d1, d2, det, pn, tail, vdd, vref,
*     vss, cb2, cb3) gets its own real star-hub R (+ ground C to `vsubs`,
*     + net-to-net coupling C) from `pex_extract_report.json`'s
*     `parasitics` block (`r_count: 77, c_count: 13, cc_count: 22`,
*     `total_resistance_ohm: 869.74`, `total_capacitance_ff: 261.13`) --
*     the largest wire-parasitic set of any experiment in this tree, being
*     the whole assembled block rather than one leaf cell.
*     `sim/tools/dump_pex_wire_parasitics.py layout/bandgap_top/
*     bandgap_top.pex.spice` emits this block mechanically (after the
*     `FB|OUT`/`IN_N|SNS1`/`IN_P|SNS2` -> `fb`/`sns1`/`sns2` renames this
*     file's header documents above) -- use it to regenerate/cross-check
*     rather than hand-transcribing.

.lib "/home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerHBT.lib" hbt_typ
.lib "/home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib" mos_sf
.lib "/home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib" res_typ

* Same convergence aids sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt's own template needs at the
* same near-singular early instant on the vdd ramp (see that template's
* header for the full whack-a-mole derivation) -- this bench drives the
* SAME three co-simulated DUTs through the SAME kind of ramp, so it
* inherits the same numerical stiffness.
.options temp=-40 tnom=27 rshunt=1e9 gmin=1e-9 reltol=5e-3

* FIXTURE -- transient supply ramp: vdd ramps 0 -> VDD over 200 us and holds
* to 3 ms, same shape sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt uses, so vref can be measured
* at two separated time points (2 ms, 3 ms) and confirmed settled.
Vvdd vdd 0 PWL(0 0 200u 3.63 3m 3.63)
Vvss vss 0 dc 0
* Ground reference for every net's own parasitic capacitance below
* (pex_extract_report.json's own convention, matching
* sim/core-open-loop-bias-pex's Rvsubs_dctie fixture) -- NOT the same net as
* vss: vsubs is an isolated ~1 TOhm-tied node, used only as the "far plate"
* for ground caps, with zero DC effect on the circuit.
Rvsubs_dctie vsubs 0 1e12

* DUT -- bandgap_core devices, extracted from layout/bandgap_top/
* bandgap_top.pex.spice (M$12-M$17, R$18/R$19) except XQ1-XQ3 (spliced,
* see file header). Each MOS/resistor keeps its extracted per-terminal
* wire-parasitic hub node; ng=1/m=1/b=0 restored on each so this bench's
* per-point netlist snapshot compares equal to design/netlist/
* bandgap_core.spice's own device signature (extra as/ad/ps/pd tolerated,
* see check_evidence_formats.py's dut_signature() docstring).
XM1 vdd__t14 fb__t6 sns1__t2 vdd__t11 sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1 as=4p ad=4p ps=20.8u pd=20.8u
XQ1 sns1 sns1 vss vss npn13G2 Nx=1
XM2A vdd__t7 fb__t5 sns2__t0 vdd__t8 sg13_hv_pmos w=9u l=1u ng=1 m=1 as=3.6p ad=3.6p ps=18.8u pd=18.8u
XM2B vdd__t20 fb__t8 sns2__t1 vdd__t18 sg13_hv_pmos w=1u l=1u ng=1 m=1 as=0.4p ad=0.4p ps=2.8u pd=2.8u
